Zero-X house style (neuroncli/auth-server/src/house-style.js)
-------------------------------------------------------------
The short style preface that the Zero-X gateway adds to coding-agent requests
(docs.html#house-style, neuroncli/auth-server/docs/HOUSE_STYLE.md) is original
text written in Zero-X's own words. It copies no text from the projects below.
Its ideas were inspired by their public descriptions:

- Ponytail, a rule set that makes a coding agent write the least code that
  works: https://github.com/DietrichGebert/ponytail (original) and the fork
  https://github.com/dkfish/ponytail. MIT licence.
  Inspired the "Economy" section (does it need to exist, does the repository,
  standard library or platform already cover it, only then new code).
- gstack by Garry Tan, role-based workflows for planning, building, review and
  shipping: https://github.com/garrytan/gstack. MIT licence.
  Inspired the "Build discipline" section (small verified steps, run the tests,
  read before editing).
- Hallmark by Nutlope, an anti-slop UI design skill:
  https://github.com/Nutlope/hallmark, and the anti-slop skill that the Neuron
  client bundles. MIT licence.
  Inspired the "Design taste" section (choose a deliberate direction first,
  avoid default generic AI page patterns, real content, accessible layouts).

Because no text from these projects is copied or vendored here, their licence
notices are not required for this code. If text from any of them is ever added
to the gateway, its licence file and copyright line must be added to this
notice in the same change. The Neuron client bundles those skills, with their
licences, in its own repository.

The names above belong to their authors. Zero-X is not affiliated with them.
